## Exercise: Implement API Hashing for Function Resolution

API hashing resolves Windows API functions by hash instead of name, preventing import table detection.

```c
// ROR13 hash function - common in shellcode
DWORD ROR13Hash(const char* functionName) {
    DWORD hash = 0;
    while (*functionName) {
        hash = (hash >> 13) | (hash << 19);  // Rotate right 13
        hash += *functionName;
        functionName++;
    }
    return hash;
}

